  "evidence": [
    "Pinned full root decode and independent owner review prove seven init/fini pairs: Radio60D060..60D076/60D080..60D09F and60D0A0..60D0B6/60D0C0..60D0DF; Check60E5F0..60E606/60E610..60E62F and60E630..60E646/60E650..60E66F; File613790..6137A6/6137B0..6137CF,6137D0..6137E6/6137F0..61380F,613810..613826/613830..61384F. Original startup calls Sprite5E37E0 and registers paired cleanup through645398. Cleanup sets its own shared bit BEFORE direct Sprite::close5E3820; all endpoints exclusive, no padded extent.",
    "Three distinct guard bytes are Radio9B8EF0 masks1/2, Check9B8F58 masks1/2 and File9B9014 masks1/2/4. Preserve independent byte storage, upper bits and no guard resets or lazy startup. Original zero-fill storage establishes initial zero, not file-backed initializer bytes. Current source and physical COFF positively identify all seven actual Sprite globals and class/FileWin consumers. Preserve existing unguarded explicit close_class/close order independently of guarded atexit.",
    "Authorize owner-local chosen aligned trivial storage and placement Sprite lifetimes at offset zero, with no extra instance fields. Wrapper destructor must preserve direct close effect exactly once with guard set first and no automatic duplicate Sprite destruction. Qualified actual Sprite destruction is valid only while the source destructor remains solely close and fresh physical output confirms direct close relocation. These types are chosen implementation, not recovered original class names, enclosing allocations, inheritance or original-header proof.",
    "RadioButton and CheckBox public declarations and all consumers must migrate consistently; CheckButtonDefaultA24/A28 and RadioButtonDefault1/2 and CheckBoxDefault1/2 must retain direct static pointer storage with fresh COFF relocation proof and no new initializer roots. No macro aliases, original-address calls, accessor-initialized global references or guessed padding. FileWin storage remains private and preserves1,0,2 declaration/explicit close order, with reverse registered shutdown.",
    "Native object replacement must preserve seven immutable original object identities, symbols and any bounded initializer obligations exactly, changing only current member owner/path to proven offset-zero raw storage; separate start-only guard bindings need fresh resulting physical symbols. Never manually edit ORIGINAL or bank unmeasured claims. FileWin native overlays under both comparison flag sets confirm guard-before-direct-close masks1/2/4 and generated registration closure; generated startup is split across helper functions and is not claimed original-byte equivalent.",
    "Before C++ commit require entire four-owner before/current measurements and relevant header consumers, complete all-source identity/claim/object continuity, fresh complete application compile/link, physical constructor/callback/guard/receiver and selected linked startup order/static default-pointer checks, actual lifecycle/mask/reentry damage controls and independent actual-diff review. Preserve source work and historical restoration obligations through coordinator-reviewed matching regressions. No game/automatic acceptance, complete cross-TU ordering, original naming/allocation, unwinding equivalence, linked retained selection or runtime proof is granted. No edits outside this task without separately expanded scope."
  ],
